# Docker COPY does not honour .gitignore. Without this file, `docker build`
# from a working clone bakes whatever is on the operator's disk into the image,
# including the two things that must never leave the machine:
#
#   inventory/hosts   is gitignored precisely because it names real servers
#   reports/          are audit results for those servers, findings and all
#
# The published image is built by CI from a fresh checkout, where neither
# exists, so this protects the local build that someone then pushes by hand.
ansible-hardening/inventory/hosts
ansible-hardening/reports/
reports/
*.json
!ansible-hardening/**/*.json

# Build and VCS noise, which also keeps the image small.
.git/
.github/
node_modules/
.venv*/
*.tar.gz
bantou96-tombstone/
mnt/
